# RU(a + b), the smallest number of the format not below the exact sum, for every pair of finite
# numbers (milestone2.md, "Rounding a sum down and up"): the rounded sum, one step up when its
# exact error is positive. At an overflow the error term is the infinity of the opposite sign:
# +inf for a sum that overflows upward, -Omega for one that overflows downward (the format with
# overflow). An infinite or NaN operand gives the sum of IEEE 754.
kernel:        add_up_1
input:         a
input:         b
output:        r
value:         a+b
ensures:       rounded r up
min_precision: 2
source:        the rounded sum and the sign of its exact error (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
theorem:       proofs/theories/DirectedSum.v add_up_1_correct
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeDirected.v add_up_1_ieee_correct
cone_exempt:   r is s or succ(s), chosen by select, and succ(-inf) is finite; the rounded claim states the output for infinite and NaN operands

(s, e) = two_sum_ord(a, b)
n      = lt(0, e)
q      = succ(s)
r      = select(n, q, s)
